<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys 7,000/T July 6-20 MTBE at $270/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 7,000/T July 6-20 MTBE at $270/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought 7,000-tonnes of methyl tertiary butyl ether (MTBE) for delivery July 6-20 to Kaohsiung or Keelung at $270 per tonne, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender for the gasoline octane enhancer, closed May 26 and was valid for two days.</p>
<p>Some traders said Saudi Basic Industries Corp (SABIC) won the tender but company sources said they have not received any confirmation from CPC.</p>
<p>CPC's last tender, for June 10-24 delivery, was awarded to Italian producer Ecofuel at a lower price of $267 per tonne on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
